# Claude Code runtime
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Python lockfile — BASE TEMPLATE ONLY.
# The template ships no uv.lock: it pins the root project by name, which is the literal
# {{PROJECT_SLUG}} until setup.sh runs. setup.sh generates the lock AND deletes this rule,
# because an instantiated project MUST commit it — every Dockerfile does
# `COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock ./` and builds with `uv sync --frozen`, so a deploy from a
# clone without the lock fails. See how-to/src/TEMPLATE-TOKENS.md.
uv.lock

